### Smalltalk01
conversation-smalltalk01-line1-a = Fair weather today, wouldn't you say?
conversation-smalltalk01-line1-b = Aye, a fine day. May it stay this calm till dusk.

conversation-smalltalk01-line2-a = Have you heard any news from the nearby villages?
conversation-smalltalk01-line2-b = Only rumors, friend. But rumors keep the world turning.

### Smalltalk02
conversation-smalltalk02-line1-a = Greetings. Roads seem quieter than usual.
conversation-smalltalk02-line1-b = Quiet roads are a blessing. Means fewer troubles wandering about.

conversation-smalltalk02-line2-a = Any advice for a traveler passing through?
conversation-smalltalk02-line2-b = Keep your purse close, your boots dry, and never ignore a warm hearth.

conversation-smalltalk02-line3-a = Sounds like wisdom earned the hard way.
conversation-smalltalk02-line3-b = In these lands, that's the only way wisdom comes.

### Casual Greetings
greeting-casual-hello = Hello there, friend.
greeting-casual-response = Good day to you! How goes your work?
greeting-casual-how-are-you = I'm well, thank you. The weather favors us today.
greeting-casual-im-fine = That it does. May your labors be light.

### MorningGreeting
conversation-morning-greeting-initiator = Good morning. How did you sleep?
conversation-morning-greeting-responder = Not bad, thank you. Hope the day will be peaceful.
